WEBVTT

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:10.541
♪ Onward Christian soldiers... ♪

00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:13.250
(Gina) 'They came from all walks of life.

00:00:15.041 --> 00:00:18.625
'But all any of them found was death.'

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.416
(Bubbling)

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.708
My father was different.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.083
Mama died when I was young,
so it was always just us.

00:00:27.208 --> 00:00:29.708
He was determined to beat the curse,

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:34.541
'but when he heard of Rumi Rock,
it took hold of him.

00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:37.333
'He disappeared into the jungle.

00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:41.083
'And I was left alone.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.541
'For years.

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:51.041
'When he returned...'

00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:52.333
(Panting)

00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:53.291
Gina!

00:00:53.416 --> 00:00:57.958
(Gina) '...he promised he would keep away
from the jungle and its ghosts.

00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:02.458
'He would stick to the river
and never love gold more than me.

00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:03.875
'I believed him.'

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:05.958
Seems I was a fool.

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:09.000
- Oh, Gina!
- Mmm! (Chuckles)

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:10.541
- Why, what is it?
- Nothing.

00:01:10.666 --> 00:01:15.041
No, just goes to show you should never trust
a handsome riverboat captain.

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:17.625
- I never said he was handsome.
- You were thinking it!

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.625
Now he is haunted
by the ghosts of ancestors

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.291
and will do anything to get his gold.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:27.166
I must get you and Paddington to safety.

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:29.083
Where is Paddington?

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.791
(Roaring)

00:01:33.916 --> 00:01:35.583
(Echoing roar)

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:39.458
(Echoing roar)

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:41.750
This way, Mr Hunter!

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:46.083
We'll follow her roars,
and we'll find her in no time!

00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:53.875
(Gonzalo) 'Do it. Cabotos don't share!'

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.125
We're getting close, Mr Hunter.

00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:12.583
And you're sure the river taxi service
will have rescued the Browns by now?

00:02:12.708 --> 00:02:15.708
- Yes.
- Oh, that is a relief.

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:18.833
Mr Brown did have
some rather wet socks.

00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:23.500
One more push,
and we'll be with Aunt Lucy.

00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:27.208
Hey! What's with all the chitchat?
Get moving!

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:29.291
I know what I have to do.

00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:33.500
Is everything... all right, Mr Hunter?

00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:36.041
Yes...

00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:40.791
There are just expectations
from my family.

00:02:40.916 --> 00:02:43.875
Oh. I didn't know you had other family.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.708
Hmm...
Do you see them much?

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.375
All the time, yes.

00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:52.250
How lovely.

00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:54.625
You know how families can be.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.208
Yes. Well, sort of.

00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:01.541
The only family I've known
is the Browns and Aunt Lucy.

00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:06.916
Before that, all I remember is
my parents died when I was very young.

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:10.458
Boo-hoo! It's a sob story!

00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:15.541
How about we cheer ourselves up
with a bowl of bear stew?

00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:17.958
- No, we can't eat him...
- Huh?

00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:20.583
- ...yet.
- What?

00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:23.833
(All repeat) What?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.583
You said something
about... eating someone.

00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:31.833
Did I?

00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:35.583
Probably it's just... the altitude.

00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:37.458
Oh. Right.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.791
Shall we get back
to finding Aunt Lucy?

00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:41.583
Yes.

00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:46.083
(Gonzalo) Don't lose your nerve.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.708
Maybe there is another way.

00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:53.125
We are too close for you to throw it
all away with your stupid feelings.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.333
Stick to the plan!

00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:59.958
You follow the bear, you find the gold,
you eat bear stew.

00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:03.333
Follow bear! Find gold! Eat stew!

00:04:03.916 --> 00:04:05.541
Bear, gold, stew!

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:13.916
Bear, gold, stew.

00:04:14.041 --> 00:04:16.083
(Paddington) Are you coming,
Mr Hunter?

00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:18.625
Right... right behind you.

00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:26.625
I can see the camp fire. It's not far.
On the other side of the valley.

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:31.000
But the bridge is down.

00:04:33.291 --> 00:04:34.916
Papa...

00:04:36.791 --> 00:04:41.708
How do we feel
about crossing over... that?

00:04:46.666 --> 00:04:48.833
We need a miracle.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.708
(Aircraft overhead)

00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:09.958
- (Judy) Look, it's Mrs Bird!
- (Jonathan) Yes!

